# 01. Document Purpose

This document converts the AEGIS architecture into an implementation-level functional specification.

It defines what each of the 13 AEGIS screens must do, what information each screen is responsible for, how users interact with it, what system state it reads, what state it may change, how it connects to other screens, and what constitutes completion.

This document is intended to become a primary source of truth for:

- product design
- UX design
- UI implementation
- frontend engineering
- backend engineering
- state management
- mock-data construction
- testing
- AI-assisted implementation
- stakeholder review

The document must be read together with:

1. AEGIS Master Architecture
2. AEGIS Domain Model + Global State Architecture
3. AEGIS User Flow + Operational Journey Architecture

If a later document conflicts with these foundational documents, the conflict must be explicitly identified and resolved rather than silently overridden.

---

# 02. Product Definition

AEGIS is a high-stakes decision-support and operational resilience system for healthcare, biosecurity, biotechnology, pandemic preparedness, and related expert environments.

AEGIS helps users move through a continuous operational cycle:

```text
SENSE
  ↓
DETECT
  ↓
DISCOVER
  ↓
ASSESS
  ↓
INVESTIGATE
  ↓
UNDERSTAND
  ↓
CONTAIN
  ↓
RESPOND
  ↓
RECOVER
  ↓
LEARN
  ↓
PREPARE
```

The interface is therefore not a collection of independent dashboards.

It is:

> **One operational system represented through 13 specialized perspectives.**

