# 05. Global Functional Rules

Every screen must follow these rules.

## FR-GLOBAL-001 — Shared Operational Reality

All screens operate against the same underlying AEGIS global state.

A user moving between screens must see consistent event state.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-002 — Navigation Does Not Equal State Mutation

Opening a screen, selecting a navigation item, or moving through the application must not automatically change the operational state of an event.

State changes require explicit system or user actions.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-003 — Context Preservation

When navigating between relevant screens, AEGIS must preserve applicable:

- active event
- threat
- risk state
- investigation state
- selected case
- transmission context
- containment state
- response state
- recovery state
- preparedness context
- evidence context
- uncertainty/confidence information
- relevant timestamps

---

## FR-GLOBAL-004 — Observation Is Not Confirmation

A detected anomaly must not automatically be presented as a confirmed biological threat.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-005 — Recommendation Is Not Execution

A system recommendation must remain distinguishable from an authorized or executed action.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-006 — Inference Is Not Fact

Potential relationships and hypotheses must remain distinguishable from confirmed findings.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-007 — Every State Change Is Traceable

Every meaningful operational state change must have an identifiable cause and timestamp.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-008 — New Evidence Can Change Understanding

AEGIS must allow new evidence to alter previous assessments without destroying historical context.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-009 — Recovery Does Not Stop Monitoring

Recovery remains an active monitored state until the event reaches its defined terminal condition.

---

## FR-GLOBAL-010 — Completed Events Remain Valuable

Historical events must remain usable for preparedness, analysis, and institutional learning.

---

# 06. Global Interaction Model

All meaningful AEGIS interactions fall into these categories:

```text
VIEW
SELECT
FILTER
EXPAND
COMPARE
INVESTIGATE
ASSESS
RECOMMEND
AUTHORIZE
EXECUTE
VERIFY
UPDATE
NAVIGATE
```

The system must never hide a consequential state change inside a generic interaction.

