# 36. Functional Definition of Done

The AEGIS product requirements are considered sufficiently implemented only when the system can demonstrate:

### Detection

A meaningful abnormal signal can enter the AEGIS operational lifecycle.

### Discovery

The system can distinguish candidate threats from raw anomalies.

### Threat Understanding

The user can establish a coherent threat picture.

### Risk

The user can assess operational significance.

### Investigation

The user can investigate evidence and hypotheses.

### Case Analysis

The user can inspect relevant cases and relationships.

### Transmission

The user can understand potential transmission pathways while preserving uncertainty.

### Containment

The user can distinguish proposed, authorized, active, and verified interventions.

### Response

The user can monitor active actions and their outcomes.

### Recovery

The user can assess stabilization against appropriate context.

### Preparedness

The user can convert event learning into future resilience.

### Research

The user can access supporting analytical/scientific context without bypassing operational controls.

### Executive Oversight

A strategic stakeholder can understand organizational risk and readiness.

### System Integrity

The complete operational context survives navigation across the 13 screens.

### State Integrity

All screens reflect the same underlying global state.

### Safety

Recommendations, authorizations, executions, inferences, and confirmed findings remain clearly differentiated.

### Traceability

Meaningful operational changes can be reconstructed from system history.

