# 38. Final Product Contract

The AEGIS interface exists to help qualified users move from:

> **Something changed.**

to:

> **We understand what changed.**

to:

> **We understand the risk.**

to:

> **We have investigated the evidence.**

to:

> **We understand possible transmission.**

to:

> **We can coordinate containment and response.**

to:

> **We can observe whether the response is working.**

to:

> **We can determine whether recovery is occurring.**

to:

> **We can learn from the event and strengthen future preparedness.**

That is the functional contract of AEGIS.

Every future feature, component, API, state transition, screen interaction, AI-generated implementation, and engineering decision must be traceable to this contract.

**If it cannot be traced to an operational requirement, it does not belong in the core AEGIS system.**
